\f0\fs24\sa120
{\b\fs36 Workspace Help}\par
Workspace is the NextBSD file manager. Each File Viewer window shows one folder, with the Locations list on the left, the path of the folder above the files, and a status line at the bottom.\par
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 Moving around}\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Double-click a folder to open it. Back, Forward, Up and Home are at the left of the toolbar, and in the Go menu.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Click the path above the files to jump to any folder that contains this one.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Go \u8594  Go to Folder\u8230  takes a path. Tab completes folder names, and the field's menu remembers recent folders.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  File \u8594  New Window and Open Folder in New Window give you another viewer with its own history.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 Views}\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  List shows name, size, kind and date; click a column title to sort by it. Columns shows the folder hierarchy side by side. Icons shows large icons; View \u8594  Larger Icons and Smaller Icons change their size.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  View \u8594  Show Hidden Files shows names that start with a dot. Folders First keeps folders at the top.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Pictures and movies show thumbnails, which you can turn off in Preferences.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 The Locations list}\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Local User holds your home folder and its standard folders, plus the Trash. Domains holds Local, Network and System. Volumes lists mounted disks.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Dropping files on a location copies them there. Right-click a favorite to remove it from the list.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 Selecting and opening}\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Click to select; Shift-click selects a range and Command-click adds or removes one item. Edit \u8594  Select All selects everything.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Double-click or press Return on a file to open it in its application. When no application is saved for that kind of file, Workspace asks which one to use.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  File \u8594  Open With\u8230  lists the applications with their icons: those that open this kind of file come first. Check \u8220 Always open \u8230  files with this application\u8221  to remember the choice; the chooser shows a saved choice with a Reset button. Other\u8230  finds an application that isn\u8217 t listed.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 Renaming and new folders}\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Select an item and press Return, or click its name a second time, to edit the name in place. Return keeps the new name; Escape keeps the old one.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  File \u8594  New Folder makes a folder called New Folder and lets you name it at once.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 Copying and moving}\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Dragging copies. Edit \u8594  Copy and Paste copy too. To move, use Edit \u8594  Cut and then Paste, or Edit \u8594  Move To\u8230  and pick the folder.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Duplicate makes a copy next to the original, called \u8220 notes copy.txt\u8221 , then \u8220 notes copy 2.txt\u8221 .\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  A copy or move that takes more than a moment shows the Processes window: what is happening, a progress bar, the item being handled, and a Stop button. Edit \u8594  Cancel Work stops it from the keyboard. Stopping keeps the items already finished, and leaves the item in progress as it was.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  When an item with the same name is already there, Workspace shows both, with their sizes and dates, and asks: Keep Both gives the new one a number, Skip leaves it out, Replace puts the new one in place, and Stop ends the operation. Check Apply to all to answer once for the rest.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 Trash and deleting}\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Edit \u8594  Move to Trash moves items to the Trash in your home folder. Open Trash in the Locations list to get them back by moving them out.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Delete Permanently removes items at once, after asking. It can\u8217 t be undone.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Edit \u8594  Undo reverses the last rename, move within the same disk, or new empty folder, as long as nothing has changed since.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 Searching}\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Type in the search field at the top right. With This Folder chosen beside it, it narrows the list to names that contain what you typed. With Subfolders, it searches every folder inside this one and lists what it finds with its location.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  View \u8594  Search (Command-F) puts the cursor in the field. Press Escape or clear the field to see the folder again.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Search matches names only, not what is inside files.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 Get Info}\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  File \u8594  Get Info (Command-I) opens the Inspector, which follows whatever you select. It shows the icon, name, kind, size, location and dates. Type a new name and press Return to rename.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Its owner, group and Read, Write and Execute boxes change who may use the item; click Apply to make the change. Only an item\u8217 s owner may change its permissions, and only an administrator may change its owner. Select several items for a summary of them all.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 How Workspace keeps your files safe}\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Workspace never replaces an item silently. When you choose Replace, the old item is kept beside the new one, named \u8220 Workspace replaced item\u8230 \u8221 , until you remove it. Folders are replaced, never merged.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  A copy is written somewhere private first and only appears when it is complete, so a stopped or failed copy never leaves half a file behind.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Moving to another disk copies first, checks the copy, and only then removes the original. If anything changed in the meantime, the original is kept and Workspace tells you where.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  When something can\u8217 t be done, one message lists each item and the reason. When everything works, Workspace says nothing.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\sb240\sa80{\b\fs28 Touchpad and keyboard}\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Tap with one finger to click; click or tap with two fingers for the menu you\u8217 d get with a right click (on items in the Locations list, for example). Tap and then drag to drag files, or turn on three-finger drag.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Scroll with two fingers; the list keeps going after you lift them and stops when you touch the touchpad again. Natural scrolling can be turned on in WindowServer\u8217 s settings.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Pinching to change the icon size and swiping with two fingers to go back and forward in a File Viewer are planned.\par\pard\sa120
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa100 \u8226  Menu shortcuts use the Command key. On a PC keyboard that is the Start (Windows) key.\par\pard\sa120
}
